TTYCHATTER C COMMAND-LINE CLIENT
================================

This directory contains the traditional Unix command-line C implementation of
ttychatter.

It is intentionally different from the Python ncurses interface.  The ncurses
client is the full-screen terminal application.  This C client is the classic
Unix tool: it reads an input file and appends output to a session file.

    ttychatter input.txt output.log

The output file is also the session state.  Reusing the same output file resumes
the conversation by sending recent turns as context.

Interactive mode
----------------

The C client also includes a line-oriented interactive mode for parity with the
Bash clients:

    ttychatter --interactive session.log

Interactive mode accepts colon commands such as :help, :models, :attach,
:editor, :memory, and :quit.  It is deliberately not a curses UI.  It exists so
users can keep chatting without preparing a new input file for every turn.

Build requirements
------------------

Debian/Ubuntu/ChromeOS Linux:

    sudo apt-get install build-essential pkg-config libcurl4-openssl-dev libjson-c-dev ca-certificates gnupg

Build:

    make

Run:

    ./ttychatter --help

Quick demo
----------

Demo mode does not need an API key and does not contact OpenRouter:

    ./ttychatter --demo --models
    ./ttychatter --demo --interactive demo.log

File workflow
-------------

    cat > input.txt
    Explain Unix pipes in one paragraph.
    ^D

    ./ttychatter --demo input.txt session.log
    less session.log

API-key setup
-------------

Encrypted storage is recommended:

    ./ttychatter --set-api-key --gpg

Plaintext config storage is also available:

    ./ttychatter --set-api-key

Read WALKTHROUGH for a complete guide.
